 "answer": "Use **`pg_relation_size()`** on the index name. pgvector's indexes (HNSW and IVFFlat) are regular Postgres relations, so the standard size functions work on them. pgvector doesn't add its own size function.\n\n```sql\nSELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size('your_index_name'));\n```\n\nRelated functions:\n\n- `pg_indexes_size('your_table')` returns the combined size of all indexes on a table.\n- `pg_total_relation_size('your_table')` includes the table, its indexes, and TOAST data.",
